[ ] Unwind projection from the live file (file is all-materialized) =occurrence-surface $REVERSAL of the shipped atomic lane (README design notes 2026-07-26 cont. 2). Remove extend_with_projected_occurrences from the load path; load_domain_model stops unioning occurrences into the action list; query/CLI/LSP see only materialized actions and the materialized-vs-projected seam disappears with the thing that needed it. The recurrence engine (expand_occurrences, deviation read/write, frame fix) SURVIVES — its output now feeds the write-path stamper and the future calendar projection, not a load-time union.$ !2 #019f962c-ba5a-7732-ad24-df6fceadea53
    >[ ] Re-home projection to future (calendar) and past (analytics) $Projection survives only as a query concern, never a core data-model piece. Future occurrences render in a read-only calendar view; past completions surface as analytics over archive/. HARD RULE: projection must never feed an index-shape query (results resolving to file:line:col to jump to/edit) — a projected occurrence has no line, so it would break the qflist as a first-class EDITING surface. The .actions file stays all-materialized; the nvim virtual-line gymnastics are obviated because present occurrences are real lines.$ !3 <occurrence-ops #019f962d-1f15-7c23-82d5-e1c8f2a652e0
    >[x] Seal the projection to sync leak $Sync reconciles owned artifacts only; a projected occurrence has no standalone resource to reconcile and no line for apply_sync to locate. sync_calendar now loads a window-0 model (Projection::without_occurrences / ctx.load_model_materialized) so occurrences are structurally absent from plan_sync, not filtered by a fragile flag. Regression-locked in workspace_store.rs. Relates to the two-assembly-sites debt in =occurrence-view.$ #019f9bdf-bad8-7940-a77e-98be6bf8b04e
[ ] Build the present-stamping lane (atomic and templated) =stamping-lane ~ $The single materialized lane — the two-lane split (project atomic / stamp templated) collapses (README 2026-07-26 cont. 2). On the write path a generator stamps the PRESENT due occurrence: atomic = a synthesized childless root from the master VTODO (SUMMARY->title, CATEGORIES->contexts, PRIORITY->priority, id = occurrence UUIDv5 = hash(plan UID, slot)); templated = the same root + the template step-forest grafted beneath it via parent_override in instantiate_template. template: only adds children. GUARDRAIL: never materialize the future — one occurrence per plan (the present); the next is generated on completion reading the RRULE fresh, so no stale future drifts.$ !2 +caldav #019fa019-079f-7681-bb22-d64ab1a9f78c
    >[ ] Stamp the present occurrence on the write path $LANDED 2026-07-26 (atomic, e2e-proven): the single-token generator. next_active_slot (expand.rs) + shared stage_plan_token stamp the PRESENT due slot into the plan's charter .actions, keyed by id = hash(plan UID, slot), with the (plan_id, slot) link in PlansSyncStore. Wired into apply_sync (reconcile.rs), rides its lock + PendingBatch, idempotent while a token is live, jump-forward on advance, self-heals a raw-completed token on the next sync. REMAINING: graft the template step-forest for templated plans (only the atomic childless root is stamped today); a catch-up cap is mooted by single-token + jump-forward.$ !2 +caldav #019fa019-3db7-7a13-8ae1-88937dd3ccdf
    >[ ] Snapshot plan-lineage onto the archived instance at completion $A completion is an immutable fact and must be self-contained. At crystallization (completion/archival) snapshot the SEMANTIC edge onto the archived instance: realizes plan-M at temporal position T, plus a human label so it survives the plan being deleted. Do NOT reverse-derive from the current RRULE (may be edited/deleted since) — the invoice-snapshots-price-at-sale principle. Layer-sensitive: while live, lineage is derived from the current rule (sync-store cache stands); the snapshot happens only at the phase transition. Snapshot the semantic edge, never the occurrence-id hash.$ !3 +caldav #019fa019-3dd0-7993-bcae-c0abfbf8f60d
[ ] Add a delete verb, distinct from close/cancel $Consequence of the fact-model: there is no immutability invariant (unenforceable across hand-editable plaintext + foreign CalDAV clients + eventually-consistent sync, so declaring it would be a lie). close/cancel are STATE TRANSITIONS (the fact persists, status changes); delete is RETRACTION FROM HISTORY (erase the thing). The user declares intent via the verb; the system does not infer human-vs-machine provenance. Safe because graphd degrades gracefully over a tolerant world (dangling refs / missing nodes / partial reads) — a deleted fact is a hole a projection absorbs. History-preserving stays the default by convention; delete is the deliberate, higher-friction exception. NOTE: likely a general workspace/action-lifecycle verb, not caldav-specific — may belong in a core charter; seeded here because the fact-model that motivates it is documented in this README.$ !3 +caldav #019fa019-5d05-7ee0-a09a-b4e20c2a304a
